<title>UK: Kvaerner cuts 137 jobs at Clydebank unit.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner cuts 137 jobs at Clydebank unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kvaerner Energy, part of international diversified business group Kvaerner ASA, said on Wednesday it is cutting 137 jobs at its thermal power division at Clydebank, Scotland.  </p>
<p>Chris Packard, president of Kvaerner Energy, said it was hoped that the total number of compulsory redundancies might be reduced by transferring some staff to the energy division's sister company in Oslo.</p>
<p>&quot;Continuing intense competition in the market-place and a lack of new orders has forced the company to make this decision,&quot; said Packard in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;At the same time, we are restructuring the business to maximise our competitive position and we're working hard to win new business in the global markets in which we operate.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
